优化-并发提取 → dependency analysis, topological sort, critical path analysis, concurrency extraction from SSA graph\n**S5**: 自动调优-Tile size/thread block/unroll factor搜索 → AutoTVM, Triton Autotuner, XLA HLO cost model\n**S6**: 自动调优-硬件在环调优 → hardware-in-the-loop, evolutionary search, measured tuning\n**S7**: 硬件侧重 → GPU occupancy vs concurrent kernel, NPU compute density vs tile selection, accelerator fixed dataflow vs graph transformation\n\nNow, for each node I need to search across the four directories. Let me start with the searches. I'll do them in batches to be efficient.\n\nGiven the large number of searches needed, let me use the Workflow tool to parallelize this. Actually, let me think about this more carefully.\n\nThe user included the keyword \"workflow\" in their message. Let me use the Workflow tool to orchestrate this efficiently. But actually, looking at the skill instructions more carefully, this is a skill invocation for `learning-experiment-from-notes-answer`. The skill says I should follow the workflow step by step.\n\nLet me reconsider - the system reminder says I should use the Workflow tool because \"workflow\" or \"workflows\" keyword was detected. But the skill instructions are explicit about the step-by-step process. Let me just follow the skill instructions directly since they're very detailed about what to do.\n\nActually wait, re-reading: \"The user included the keyword \"workflow\" or \"workflows\", which means you should use the Workflow tool to fulfill their request.\" This is a system instruction. But the skill itself has a very specific workflow defined in it. Let me think about whether using the Workflow tool makes sense here.\n\nThe skill instruction defines a very specific search-then-read-then-write workflow. Using the Workflow tool might help parallelize some searches. But the skill also requires careful sequential reasoning - you need to read notes before writing answers.\n\nLet me just follow the skill instructions step by step. The k