{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"2442ac93-8c97-484e-9c67-0bc5df26f580","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have a substantial body of evidence from the vault. Let me consolidate the key findings and start writing the answer.\n\nLet me organize what I have by logical node:\n\n**S1: 子图切分与设备放置 (Subgraph Partitioning & Device Placement)**\n- NetMoE paper: Dynamic sample placement for MoE training, device placement via ILP\n- FlexMoE: Dynamic device placement for MoE\n- Lazarus: Adaptive expert placement with replicas, fault-tolerant elastic MoE training\n- ELK compiler: Two-level inductive operator scheduling for ICCA chips, preload-execution overlap\n- Note evidence is mostly about MoE expert placement, not compiler-level subgraph partitioning per se\n\n**S2: 内存规划与重计算 (Memory Planning & Rematerialization)**\n- MegaScale-MoE: Holistic scheduling + Selective Activation Rematerialization (SAR), saves ~50% activation memory\n- MoEBlaze: Selective checkpointing of SiLU activation, 4× memory reduction\n- FlashAttention: Recomputation in backward pass (don't save attention matrix)\n- Mamba/SSM: Recomputation saves 8.5× IO\n- HuntKTm: Memory manager with liveness analysis, in-place memory reuse\n\n**S3: 布局优化 (Layout Optimization)**\n- RoMeo paper: Mixed precision quantization with rotated token-wise computation\n- HuntKTm: In-place operations to reuse memory of input/output tensors\n- Welder: Tile-graph scheduling for memory access optimization\n- Vertical fusion: Tile size constraints from shared memory capacity\n\n**S4: 并发提取 (Concurrency Extraction)**\n- HuntKTm: Stream scheduler automatically identifies data dependencies, places kernels into different streams, hybrid kernel+task scheduling\n- ACS: Runtime dependency checking within a scheduling window (like OoO instruction scheduling), automatic concurrent kernel scheduling for irregular graphs\n- DAG-based Batching: MoE-GEN's critical path analys